 calls  | mean_ms |  rows   | query
--------+---------+---------+--------------------------------------------------------------
     40 |  2310.0 |    1240 | SELECT c.category, count(*) FROM activity_log a JOIN courses
   1920 |    61.3 |   19200 | SELECT * FROM enrollments WHERE user_id = $1 ORDER BY create
 118400 |     4.2 |  118400 | SELECT id, password_hash FROM users WHERE lower(email) = $1

Statement: "The first row of this report is the statement that spent the most total time in the database during these 24 hours."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Total time is calls x mean: 40 x 2,310 ms = 92 s for the category report, 1,920 x 61.3 ms = 118 s for the enrollments query and 118,400 x 4.2 ms = 497 s for the sign-in lookup. Ordered by mean, the sign-in query sits at the bottom although it uses five times more database time than the report at the top (pg_stat_statements also has a total_exec_time column; order by it to see the load). Mean time answers "which query is slow when it runs", total time answers "which query costs the database most" - both are worth knowing, but a ranking by mean alone hides the frequent fast query that keeps the database busy.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_111') AND order_index = 2)
