WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_121'), 'EXPLAIN (ANALYZE) of the course progress query for course 42:

Sort  (cost=1004.71..1005.01 rows=120 width=40) (actual time=1213.054..1214.871 rows=18204 loops=1)
  Sort Key: lp.completed_at DESC
  Sort Method: quicksort  Memory: 1985kB
  ->  Nested Loop  (cost=0.99..1000.57 rows=120 width=40) (actual time=0.092..1209.330 rows=18204 loops=1)
        ->  Index Scan using enrollments_course_id_idx on enrollments e  (cost=0.43..412.10 rows=120 width=16) (actual time=0.031..21.402 rows=18204 loops=1)
              Index Cond: (course_id = 42)
              Filter: (status = ''active''::text)
              Rows Removed by Filter: 611
        ->  Index Scan using lesson_progress_user_id_course_id_idx on lesson_progress lp  (cost=0.56..4.89 rows=1 width=32) (actual time=0.058..0.064 rows=1 loops=18204)
              Index Cond: ((user_id = e.user_id) AND (course_id = 42))
Planning Time: 0.412 ms
Execution Time: 1216.022 ms

Statement: "About 1,165 ms of the 1,216 ms execution is spent inside the Index Scan on lesson_progress, even though its actual time reads only 0.064 ms."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The actual time of a node is the average for one execution, and loops=18204 says the inner side of the Nested Loop ran 18,204 times, once per enrollment row. Its total time is 0.064 ms x 18,204 = 1,165 ms. The Nested Loop''s own work is then 1,209.330 - 21.402 - 1,165.056 = about 23 ms and the Sort adds about 5.5 ms on top of its child, so the Sort at the top is not the problem even though it shows the largest number. The common misconception is to read actual time as a total and to blame the first node whose time is large: always multiply by loops and subtract the children before you decide where the time goes.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_121') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
