    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_121'), 'EXPLAIN (without ANALYZE) of the activity feed query:

EXPLAIN SELECT id, user_id, kind, created_at
FROM activity_log
WHERE kind = ''quiz_submitted''
ORDER BY created_at DESC
LIMIT 50;

Limit  (cost=0.56..41.93 rows=50 width=36)
  ->  Index Scan Backward using activity_log_created_at_idx on activity_log  (cost=0.56..2391755.12 rows=2890500 width=36)
        Filter: (kind = ''quiz_submitted''::text)

Statement: "The planner predicts that this query will run for about 42 ms."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Costs are in the planner''s own units, scaled so that reading one page sequentially costs seq_page_cost = 1.0; they are not milliseconds and plain EXPLAIN never measures or predicts time. 41.93 means the planner expects to stop after about 50/2,890,500 of the index scan''s total cost of 2,391,755 units, because LIMIT ends the scan early. Costs are for comparing alternative plans of the same query; to know how long it runs you need EXPLAIN ANALYZE (which really executes it) or the timings in pg_stat_statements. The misconception is reading cost as a duration, then being surprised when a plan with a small cost runs for seconds because the 50 matching rows are not near the end of the index.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_121') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
