WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_131'), 'A release added the activity kind ''certificate_issued'' and backfilled 1,920,000 rows into activity_log (48,000,000 rows). The statistics were gathered before the backfill:

SELECT null_frac, n_distinct, most_common_vals, most_common_freqs
FROM pg_stats WHERE tablename = ''activity_log'' AND attname = ''kind'';

 null_frac | n_distinct
-----------+------------
         0 |         12

 most_common_vals:  {lesson_viewed,lesson_completed,quiz_submitted,signed_in,enrolled,course_viewed,quiz_passed,hint_opened,badge_earned,profile_updated}
 most_common_freqs: {0.41,0.22,0.18,0.11,0.03,0.018,0.012,0.005,0.005,0.004}

EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT user_id, created_at FROM activity_log WHERE kind = ''certificate_issued'';

Bitmap Heap Scan on activity_log  (cost=1612.12..402170.40 rows=144000 width=16) (actual time=208.311..6120.877 rows=1920000 loops=1)
  Recheck Cond: (kind = ''certificate_issued''::text)
  ->  Bitmap Index Scan on activity_log_kind_idx  (cost=0.00..1576.12 rows=144000 width=0) (actual time=190.102..190.102 rows=1920000 loops=1)
        Index Cond: (kind = ''certificate_issued''::text)

Statement: "The estimate of 144,000 rows is 48,000,000 x (1 - 0.994) / (12 - 10): ''certificate_issued'' is not in the MCV list, so it gets an equal share of the rows that the list does not cover."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The ten MCV frequencies add up to 0.994 and null_frac is 0, so 0.006 of the rows have a value outside the list. n_distinct says there are 12 distinct values, 10 of them in the list, so the planner assumes the remaining 2 values share those rows equally: 0.006 / 2 = 0.003, and 0.003 x 48,000,000 = 144,000. The planner has no idea that one new value now covers 4% of the table, because the sample was taken before the backfill. The estimate is 13x too low; ANALYZE activity_log after the backfill puts ''certificate_issued'' into the MCV list with a frequency near 0.04. The misconception is that the planner looks at the data when it plans; it only looks at the last statistics sample.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_pgp_131') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
