       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_pgp_222'), 2, 'Compare the expression in the WHERE clause with the expression the index was built on: the planner only searches an index whose key is exactly the expression being compared. Then check the stored data in the tests: are all stored emails already lower case?'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_pgp_222'), 3, 'A similar case on another column: courses are looked up with WHERE lower(title) = lower(?), and an index on title is never searched. CREATE INDEX courses_title_lower ON courses (lower(title)) indexes the same expression the query compares, and EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN then shows SEARCH courses USING INDEX courses_title_lower (<expr>=?).');
