 52391 | active              | Lock   | 00:00:47 | {52310}     | INSERT INTO enrollments (user_id, course_id, status)
(... 214 more rows, all blocked_by {52310})

Statement: "The API queries are waiting because ALTER TABLE is rewriting the enrollments table; they will continue once the rewrite finishes, so the fix is to make the rewrite faster."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The ALTER TABLE is not doing any work: its wait_event_type is Lock and pg_blocking_pids shows it is itself blocked by pid 41207, a session that ran a SELECT on enrollments 23 minutes ago and never committed (idle in transaction). That SELECT still holds an ACCESS SHARE lock until its transaction ends. ALTER TABLE needs ACCESS EXCLUSIVE, so it waits, and every later query on the table, even a plain SELECT, queues behind the waiting ALTER because its requested lock conflicts with theirs. Adding a nullable column without a default does not rewrite the table at all. The fix is to end the root blocker (fix the code that leaves the transaction open, set idle_in_transaction_session_timeout) and to run migrations with SET lock_timeout = ''3s'' and a retry, so a DDL statement that cannot get its lock gives up instead of freezing the table. The misconception is to blame the statement at the head of the visible queue instead of following blocked_by to the root.', 1, 5
